{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c1a33e65-fe87-4044-bdc1-94a7409ba49c",
    "name": "Doryoku Positions API (v1)",
    "description": "Metered public API for Uniswap v4 DeFi data — positions (PnL / APR / ROI), pools (TVL / volume / fees + positions/holders counts), and time-series charts.\n\n## Auth\nEvery request under **Positions** and **Pools** requires the `KC-APIKey` header. The collection sends it automatically from the `{{apiKey}}` variable.\n`/v1/chains` and `/v1/protocols` (the **Metadata** folder) are free and unauthenticated.\n\n## Key types\nKeys are issued as either **server** or **browser** type:\n- **server** — backend-only. Rejected (403) if a request carries an `Origin` header (i.e. is made from a browser). Use these for server-to-server calls.\n- **browser** — bound to one or more website origins (e.g. `https://app.example.com`). A browser call from any other origin is rejected (403), so a leaked key is useless on other sites.\n\nCalls from Postman / curl / a backend send no `Origin` header, so **either key type works here** — the browser binding only restricts real in-browser usage.\n\n## Setup\n1. Set the `baseUrl` collection variable to the API host (defaults to `http://localhost:3000`).\n2. The `apiKey` variable is pre-filled with your key.\n\n## Metering & limits\nEach metered call costs 1 unit (live-tunable per route). Requests are rate-limited per minute and quota-metered per month per the plan attached to the key. On 429 see the `Retry-After`, `X-RateLimit-*`, and `X-Quota-*` response headers.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": ""
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Positions",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List positions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/positions?chainId=1&protocol=uniswap-v4&sort=apr&page=1&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "positions"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "chainId",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Chain id. Default 1 (Ethereum)."
                },
                {
                  "key": "protocol",
                  "value": "uniswap-v4",
